From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 07:38:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 025/159] [ae-patch] Let navigation.openExternal open GitHub
 pull request and issue URLs

Extension pages run in an iframe with sandbox="allow-scripts", so they
cannot open a window themselves, and navigation.openExternal refused any URL
the host had not handed out ("URL was not provided by the host"). The AE
Dashboard reads its pull requests from its own routes, so its cards offered
only Copy link, and Reid (on an iPhone, 2026-09-27) had to paste every link
into Safari.

The handler now also opens a URL that isAeGithubLinkUrl accepts
(web/src/lib/aeExternalUrls.ts): exactly
https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/pull/<n> (optionally /files, /commits or
/checks) or https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/issues/<n>, with an optional
#fragment; no query, userinfo or port; owner and repo from [A-Za-z0-9._-];
the string must equal its own parsed href. Every other URL keeps the
handed-out rule, and the method still needs the navigation permission.

The upstream suite's handed-out case now uses a non-GitHub host so it still
proves that rule; useExtensionHostServices.aeGithub.test.tsx and
aeExternalUrls.test.ts cover the new path.

